n that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t),$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(3t))}{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-(3{sec}^{2}⁡(3t)))}{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{sec}^{3}⁡(3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{9},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /9}=-\\frac{1}{2}{sec}^{3}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{9})=-4.\n$$" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263126 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263127 13194139533882 true] [17592186263126 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533882 true] [17592186263126 1041 "field-1" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263126 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263127 13194139533882 true] [17592186263126 1110 #uuid "2ba405bf-b8ee-5d87-a4a7-37dc89d05b25" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263127 1034 "-4" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263127 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533882 true] [17592186263127 1111 #uuid "10b7da2b-24c5-5f48-84f0-c7179572b60b" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263128 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263129 13194139533882 true] [17592186263128 1089 "q-50018" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263128 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533882 true] [17592186263128 1100 "A curve has parametric equations $x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).$ Given that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t),$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12}.$" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263128 1113 #uuid "b7ac0d82-05be-587a-a9fe-883433fc2c18" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263128 1145 "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t),$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t))}{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}⁡(2t)}{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{csc}^{3}⁡(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}{|}_{t=\\pi /12} & =-\\frac{1}{4}{csc}^{3}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{sin}^{3}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263130 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263131 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263132 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263133 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263134 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1041 "selection" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1104 #edb/ref 17592186263134 13194139533882 true] [17592186263129 1110 #uuid "902af463-8279-57a4-91c7-95549b704ae8" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263130 1034 "-8" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533882 true] [17592186263130 1111 #uuid "f0b61dcf-3032-532b-95a5-8bb56c7ba240" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263131 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533882 true] [17592186263131 1111 #uuid "22ea0549-ce63-5505-bc83-5d96233889e8" 13194139533882 true] [17592186263132 